@page "/interview"
@inject IInterviewService InterviewService
@inject IDraftStateService DraftStateService
@inject NavigationManager NavigationManager

@*
    The interview, and this page owns none of its pieces: the journey across the top, the question,
    and the agent's rows along the foot are each their own component under Shared/Interview. What is
    left here is the only thing that is genuinely this page's — driving the state machine and
    deciding where the client goes when the map is spent.

    There is no transcript on the screen, and remembering the conversation is not the client's job
    either: it is the agent's, and it has a live AgentSession that is the real record. A second copy
    beside it would be a log to keep in step with one that already exists, in exchange for a panel
    saying what the client has just finished saying.

    Opening this page is what lights the burner. Arriving here is already the client saying what they
    came to do, so a screen that describes the interview and offers to begin it is a door in front of
    a door.

    Nothing on this page advances the interview by itself. The model decides which question comes
    next and when a step is behind it; the state machine confirms that before agreeing. The client is
    asked about their work and never about Alembic's structure, which is why the steps are named in
    their words and the word "pass" appears nowhere they can see it.
*@

<div class="alembic-page">

    @*
        Taking the work away sits on the band that says where you are — under the mark, over the rail,
        on the line the eye already travels down before it reaches the question. It is not part of
        answering, so it does not stand in the line of it; and it is not off in a corner of the
        window either, because a thing pinned away from everything else is a thing nobody meets. It is
        there from the first turn: a map dictated and lost is the same afternoon gone.
    *@
    <div class="whereabouts">
        <SaveWork />
    </div>

    @if (InterviewService.Current is not { } interviewState)
    {
        <div class="scene">
            <div class="thinking"><span>&bull;</span><span>&bull;</span><span>&bull;</span></div>
        </div>
    }
    else
    {
        <Journey State="interviewState" Established="Established" Written="Written(interviewState)" />

        @*
            The way back travels with whatever is on the table — the answer or the commit — and is a
            button of the same size beside it, because going back is the one movement of the interview
            the client decides.
        *@
        @if (Written(interviewState))
        {
            <AgentWritten State="interviewState" Busy="isBusy" OnAccept="AcceptAsync">
                <Back>
                    <StepBack State="interviewState" Busy="isBusy" OnBack="BackAsync" />
                </Back>
            </AgentWritten>
        }
        else
        {
            <Question Asked="@(interviewState.Question ?? "…")"
                      Prompting="@Prompting(interviewState)"
                      Choices="Offered(interviewState)"
                      Traits="interviewState.Traits"
                      Busy="isBusy"
                      Turn="interviewState.Exchanges"
                      OnAnswer="SendAsync"
                      OnChoose="ChooseAsync">
                <Back>
                    <StepBack State="interviewState" Busy="isBusy" OnBack="BackAsync" />
                </Back>
            </Question>
        }

        @if (interviewState.Error is not null)
        {
            <p class="severity-error">@interviewState.Error</p>
        }

    }

</div>

@code {
    private bool isBusy;
    private bool started;

    /// <summary>
    /// What the domain held before this interview: earlier sittings and uploaded configurations.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Anything on today's map is left out, agents committed a minute ago included — the map shows
    /// those in their own place, and a name in both strips reads as two intents. The fallback is left
    /// out for a different reason: it is in every domain, no agent answers it, and it is not a step
    /// of anybody's work.
    /// </remarks>
    private IEnumerable<IntentDraft> Established =>
        (DraftStateService.Current?.Intents ?? [])
            .Where(i => !string.Equals(i.Name, DomainDraft.FallbackIntent, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
            .Where(i => InterviewService.Current?.Map.Any(m =>
                            string.Equals(m.Name, i.Name, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)) != true);

    /// <summary>
    /// Whether every section is settled and the agent is waiting to be let into the domain.
    /// </summary>
    private static bool Written(InterviewState interviewState) =>
        interviewState is { Pass: InterviewPass.AgentFinalizer, ReadyForReview: true };

    /// <summary>
    /// The worked example in the answer box, shown on the first question of a step and no other.
    /// </summary>
    // An example rather than a label: somebody who has just been asked a question does not yet know
    // what a good answer looks like, and naming the material only restates the question. Each shows
    // the register, the length and the detail at once, in a trade the client does not have.
    //
    // The four are one story, told once. The first draws the boundary — the shop sells, Morgana
    // handles what comes after the order — and the others pick up where the last stopped without
    // repeating it, so a client answering in this register hands over material that does not
    // overlap with itself.
    private static string Prompting(InterviewState interviewState)
        => !interviewState.PassJustOpened ? string.Empty : interviewState.Pass switch
            {
                InterviewPass.DomainMapper =>
                    "We sell coffee online, a dozen blends, mostly on subscription. Selling is not what I "
                    + "want her for — the site does that, and roasting stays with us. It is what comes "
                    + "after the order: people writing to move a delivery, to swap what is in the next box, "
                    + "or to ask for an invoice.",

                InterviewPass.AgentModeler =>
                    "Someone wants their delivery moved, usually giving a date and their order number. We "
                    + "find their subscription, shift it, and tell them the new day. We never change the "
                    + "payment or the blend in the same breath, and we never promise a date before we know "
                    + "it can be held.",

                // The voice step has none, and that is not an omission. Its question is answered by
                // picking from the words offered under it, and a fifty-word story in the box beside
                // them would be an example of an answer nobody is being asked for.
                InterviewPass.AgentVoicer => string.Empty,

                InterviewPass.ToolkitModeler =>
                    "To do that we look the subscription up in our order system by the customer's email, "
                    + "then check with the warehouse whether the next box has already been packed. If it "
                    + "has not, we set the new date on it and a confirmation goes out by email. The packing "
                    + "status is theirs, not ours.",

                _ =>
                    "We check the subscription first, then say what can be done, then do it — never confirm "
                    + "before the change is made. One short line back, with the new day written out in "
                    + "full. We keep back which courier we use and what the shipping costs us; if the box "
                    + "has already gone, we say so and offer the one after."
            };

    /// <summary>
    /// The choices attached to the question being asked right now, if any.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// A choice belongs to the question it was asked with, so the row goes the moment one is
    /// pressed: what stands after that is the next question, and offering an answer to something
    /// already settled is worse than offering nothing.
    /// </remarks>
    private static IReadOnlyList<QuickReply>? Offered(InterviewState interviewState) =>
        interviewState.ChosenId is null ? interviewState.Choices : null;

    /// <summary>
    /// Sends a choice as the answer, and records which one was pressed.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Recorded before the round trip, so the button lights the instant it is clicked rather than
    /// after the model answers. Without it the screen shows an answer nobody typed and no trace of
    /// the gesture that produced it.
    /// </remarks>
    private Task ChooseAsync(QuickReply choice)
    {
        if (InterviewService.Current is { } interviewState)
            interviewState.ChosenId = choice.Id;

        return SendAsync(choice.Value);
    }

    private async Task SendAsync(string said)
    {
        isBusy = true;
        try { await InterviewService.AnswerAsync(said); }
        finally { isBusy = false; }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Steps back to the previous part of the interview.
    /// </summary>
    private async Task BackAsync()
    {
        isBusy = true;
        try { await InterviewService.BackAsync(); }
        finally { isBusy = false; }
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Lights the burner on arrival.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// Here rather than in <c>OnInitializedAsync</c> because the first turn of an interview is a
    /// model call on the Performance tier, and this is the first place the circuit is known to be
    /// live and the screen already drawn — so the client sees the burner lit rather than a page that
    /// arrives once the model has finished thinking. The flag keeps a re-render from starting a
    /// second one.
    /// </remarks>
    protected override async Task OnAfterRenderAsync(bool firstRender)
    {
        if (!firstRender || started || InterviewService.Current is not null)
            return;

        started = true;
        isBusy = true;
        StateHasChanged();

        try { await InterviewService.StartAsync(); }
        finally { isBusy = false; }

        StateHasChanged();
    }

    /// <summary>
    /// Lets the finished agent into the domain, and goes on to the next entry of the map.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// The review is where the interview ends, not where each agent lands: an agent is only worth
    /// weighing against the others once the others exist, and a report between every two entries of
    /// the map turns one interview into a series of errands.
    /// </remarks>
    private async Task AcceptAsync()
    {
        isBusy = true;

        try
        {
            if (!await InterviewService.AcceptAsync())
                NavigationManager.NavigateTo("review");
        }
        finally { isBusy = false; }
    }
}
